summary:
  The station list shows a saved station only when its name holds the text.

history:
  The web results leave out every station the list already holds, and the
  list's own filter read names alone. A saved station the directory found by
  its country, its language or its genre was dropped from the results and
  hidden in the list: "Example FM", filed under Estonia and jazz, stood
  nowhere under "estonia" or "jazz", and a row starred under such a search
  vanished at the click. The list now also shows the stations the answer named.

target:
  package/contents/ui/ReorderLogic.js

find:
          if (filter !== "" && found[i] !== true && SearchLogic.fold(s.name).indexOf(filter) === -1)

replace:
          if (filter !== "" && SearchLogic.fold(s.name).indexOf(filter) === -1)

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_reorderlogic.qml::test_a_saved_station_the_directory_named_shows_whatever_its_name_says
  and tests/qml/tst_reorderlogic.qml::test_a_named_station_is_found_under_another_address.
  Line-neutral.
